<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The same invoice as ubl-invoice.xml with defects planted, so you can see what
  a failing run looks like before pointing the tool at your own export. Every
  one of these is a mistake a real export makes. Rule IDs are asserted by the
  test suite, so this list cannot drift from what the tool actually reports:

    INV-021  The due date is before the issue date.
    INV-045  Payment by credit transfer with no IBAN to pay into.
    INV-038  The 19% group states VAT of 36.10 on a taxable amount of 200.00,
             which is not 19% of it.
    INV-018  ...so the document VAT total of 46.60 no longer matches the lines.
    INV-017  Gross total of 380.00 is not net plus tax.
    INV-029  ...and the amount due, which is derived from that gross, is wrong
             in turn. One typo is rarely one finding, which is the point.
-->
